Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||06-30-2001||12:26 PM||||On the solenoid connector harness, put a connection between curcuits A & B - this will cure the problem of having an engine code by cheating and lying to the computer, and it will work the same as a new unit without going out and buying a new unit||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-30-2001||12:37 PM||||But your egr valve will no longer work because now the current operating the soliniod is shorted, and vacuum will not be directed to EGR valve.  <P>W C F - You are correct thou it will trick the ecm to cancel code 32.||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||06-30-2001||01:19 PM||||these curcuits do not energize the EGR soleniod, they only activate a check velve withing the unit, therefore it is viable to simply jump the curcuits, unless you desire to spend $142.81 for a similar AC Delco unit, because the unit for the Fiero is no longer produced, you will have to use the Camaro (93-95) Solenoid, and you will have to make slight alterations to that as well||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||06-30-2001||03:41 PM||||I yoinked one from a Camaro with a 2.8 at the boneyard and it worked fine...  the mounting bracket was slightly different, but it still fits.||||reg||1
